# Sample 5 - FederatedAccess manual requests
# Start sample:
#   dotnet run --project samples/FederatedAccess -- interactive

@resource1Base = https://localhost:3012
@asBase = https://localhost:3014
@resource2Base = https://localhost:3015
@psBase = https://localhost:3013
@apBase = https://localhost:3011
@agentJwt = {{$processEnv AGENT_JWT}}

### Metadata - AP/Resource1/PS/AS/Resource2
GET {{apBase}}/.well-known/aauth-agent.json
###
GET {{resource1Base}}/.well-known/aauth-resource.json
###
GET {{psBase}}/.well-known/aauth-person.json
###
GET {{asBase}}/.well-known/aauth-access.json
###
GET {{resource2Base}}/.well-known/aauth-resource.json

# VERIFY:
#   - All return 200 OK with discovery metadata
#   - Resource 1's metadata should show its resource identifier
#   - Access Server serves aauth-access.json (not aauth-resource.json)
#   - Resource 2's metadata shows its resource identifier (accessed by R1 during call chaining)

### Step 1: R1 authorize with agent token -> resource_token
# dotnet run --project labs/scripts/AAuth.SignTool -- --jwt "$AGENT_JWT" --method POST --url "https://localhost:3012/authorize"
@r1AuthSigKey = REPLACE_SIGNATURE_KEY
@r1AuthSigInput = REPLACE_SIGNATURE_INPUT
@r1AuthSig = REPLACE_SIGNATURE

POST {{resource1Base}}/authorize
Content-Type: application/json
Signature-Key: {{r1AuthSigKey}}
Signature-Input: {{r1AuthSigInput}}
Signature: {{r1AuthSig}}

{
  "scope": "weather.read"
}

# VERIFY:
#   - 200 OK with resource_token
#   - Decode resource_token: aud points to the Access Server (not the PS directly)
#   - This is the key difference from Sample 3: federation routes through an AS

### Step 2: PS token exchange for R1 resource token -> auth token
# ⚠️ RE-SIGN REQUIRED: Generate fresh headers for the PS token endpoint.
@r1ResourceToken = REPLACE_R1_RESOURCE_TOKEN
# dotnet run --project labs/scripts/AAuth.SignTool -- --jwt "$AGENT_JWT" --method POST --url "https://localhost:3013/token"
@psTokenSigKey = REPLACE_SIGNATURE_KEY
@psTokenSigInput = REPLACE_SIGNATURE_INPUT
@psTokenSig = REPLACE_SIGNATURE

POST {{psBase}}/token
Content-Type: application/json
Signature-Key: {{psTokenSigKey}}
Signature-Input: {{psTokenSigInput}}
Signature: {{psTokenSig}}

{
  "resource_token": "{{r1ResourceToken}}"
}

# VERIFY:
#   - 200 OK with auth_token
#   - Decode auth_token: issuer is the AS (not the PS), dwk=aauth-access.json
#   - The PS discovered the AS and forwarded the exchange (PS→AS federation)
#   - This proves: the PS acts as a proxy, the AS is the actual token issuer

### Step 3: Access R1 data with auth token (expected 200)
# ⚠️ RE-SIGN REQUIRED: Generate fresh headers using the auth token.
@r1AuthToken = REPLACE_R1_AUTH_TOKEN
# dotnet run --project labs/scripts/AAuth.SignTool -- --jwt "{{r1AuthToken}}" --method GET --url "https://localhost:3012/api/data"
@r1AccessSigKey = REPLACE_SIGNATURE_KEY
@r1AccessSigInput = REPLACE_SIGNATURE_INPUT
@r1AccessSig = REPLACE_SIGNATURE

GET {{resource1Base}}/api/data
Signature-Key: {{r1AccessSigKey}}
Signature-Input: {{r1AccessSigInput}}
Signature: {{r1AccessSig}}

# VERIFY:
#   - 200 OK with Resource 1's data
#   - Signature-Key contains the AS-issued auth token

### Step 4: Call chaining through R1 /api/enriched (R1 authorizes R2 behind the scenes)
# ⚠️ RE-SIGN REQUIRED: Generate fresh headers using the auth token.
# dotnet run --project labs/scripts/AAuth.SignTool -- --jwt "{{r1AuthToken}}" --method GET --url "https://localhost:3012/api/enriched"
@enrichedSigKey = REPLACE_SIGNATURE_KEY
@enrichedSigInput = REPLACE_SIGNATURE_INPUT
@enrichedSig = REPLACE_SIGNATURE

GET {{resource1Base}}/api/enriched
Signature-Key: {{enrichedSigKey}}
Signature-Input: {{enrichedSigInput}}
Signature: {{enrichedSig}}

# VERIFY:
#   - 200 OK with combined data from Resource 1 AND Resource 2
#   - R1 acted as an agent to R2: signed a request with its own agent token
#   - The auth token for R2 contains nested "act" claims showing delegation:
#     act.sub = R1's agent ID, proving the chain Agent → R1 → R2
#   - This proves: call chaining with preserved delegation context

### Negative: unsigned call to /api/enriched (expected 401)
GET {{resource1Base}}/api/enriched

# VERIFY:
#   - 401 Unauthorized
#   - No signature headers → immediate rejection
